## Original Content
Austin-based ClearJet, an AI-enabled logistics technology startup connects shippers with unused cargo capacity on commercial flights, has raised a $25 million Edison Partners-led Series B, it tells Crunchbase News exclusively.

## Summary
ClearJet, an AI-enabled logistics technology startup, has raised $25 million in a Series B funding round led by Edison Partners to expand its platform that connects shippers with unused cargo capacity on commercial flights. This investment aims to scale their innovative service, described as the 'Uber of Cargo,' to revolutionize air freight logistics. The funding will support the development and growth of their technology-driven approach.

## Key Points
- ClearJet raised $25 million in a Series B funding round.
- Edison Partners led the investment.
- The startup uses AI to connect shippers with available cargo space on flights.
- The platform is modeled after Uber, targeting underutilized cargo capacity.
- The funding will facilitate scaling and technological advancements.


